# 24. Generate a Successful Login

If you have a test account on your own lab VM, perform a normal SSH login:

```bash
ssh <your-test-user>@localhost
```

Then check:

```bash
sudo grep "Accepted" /var/log/auth.log | tail
```

Now you can compare:

```text
Failed Authentication
        ↓
Successful Authentication
```

This connects directly to your Day 14 and Day 22 investigations.

